{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage","id":779658,"title":"Strix, Shadow Form and Damage.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-04T03:27:15-08:00","id":779658,"title":"Strix, Shadow Form and Damage.","content":"Hey all, I've been through every possible resource so I'm looking for a hand with Strix in my VTR2 game. Questions as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) Strix in Shadow Form (assume SP1). Can they actually hurt a vampire? I've assumed they are effectively just animate, sentient shadows; unable to actually do any direct harm (short of breath drinking).<br /> <br /> 2) Harming Strix in shadow form. Strix ignore all damage. Unless it's magic, or is a special power that does agg in which case it is reduced to bashing. Consider though, Claws of the Unholy, or Feeding the Crone. Both do aggravated wounds, but they're still physical attacks that can't actually touch the Strix to inflict those wounds to begin with.<br /> <br /> Any ideas or clarification would be much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6009-nathanb","name":"NathanB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:02:15-08:00","id":779680,"title":"","content":"I'm not a developer, so take what I say with a pinch of salt thrown over the shoulder:<br /> <br /> 1) Strix cannot use Breath Drinking on vampires. In Shadow Form they don't seem able to inflict physical injury, but they're largely immune to Kindred attack. This is great for terrifying scenes as the vampire is haunted by some dark thing of smoke and shadow. Their Dread Powers still affect vampires normally, and they can presumably harass the vampires with other Skills.<br /> <br /> 2) This one is going to be a judgment call for your group. Claws of the Unholy is a power born of Vitae and Kindred nature, so maybe it has the power to rend the shadow-owls\u2014only to horrify the vampire as the Strix in question seems unfazed. Or maybe they simply don't work on a shadow-form Strix and the vampire needs to pursue other methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:15:03-08:00","id":779686,"title":"","content":"Yeah, at SP1 there's not a lot a strix can do against anything directly. They can't even possess a host. So indirect is the order of the day. One idea I've had is that they could cause a motorway pile-up by obscuring the vision of a truck driver at just the right moment. Get creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:23:55-08:00","id":779694,"title":"","content":"Personally, I rule that Protean 4 claws, the Theban blood whip, as well as other magics deal their normal damage type against the strix, despite being physical attacks. There's precidence, given the Khaibit powers. Magic attacks hurt strix. I'm okay with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:38:45-08:00","id":779701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage?p=779694#post779694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I rule that Protean 4 claws, the Theban blood whip, as well as other magics deal their normal damage type against the strix, despite being physical attacks. There's precidence, given the Khaibit powers. Magic attacks hurt strix. I'm okay with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the case, then the Strix explicitly take only bashing damage from those powers, as described on page 202. Non-vampire powers might inflict normal damage, depending on how you look at it, and there's always room for personal rules options like yours to let Disciplines affect Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:55:45-08:00","id":779709,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;only deal bashing&quot; bit is nothing more than just extending one's health track, as far as I'm concerned. Yes, you can kill it, but you must have a lot of damage to put them down. The introduction of the Khaibit into the game changes everything, though, when dealing with the strix. Dealing automatic lethal damage on top of being able to hit the thing, and passing out the weapons, frankly, makes it far less of a threat when it comes to hurting them. Suddenly, we went from nigh unvulnerable, to managable. So, I opened the door a bit more. They're still an issue, but act differently enough that they're still a threat, but not one that's not as much a physical threat in shadow form. Which is something I'm okay with as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T15:57:01-08:00","id":781903,"title":"","content":"I understand that usually &quot;decide what's best for your game&quot; is the rule, but that's not entirely suitable to environment we play in. I'm really hoping to get some indication of what the RAW is intended to be. If anyone can point to some kind of semi-formal ruling, FAQ or forum post, I'd be super grateful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6009-nathanb","name":"NathanB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T02:22:04-08:00","id":782162,"title":"","content":"I'd say Claws of the Unholy definitely counts as a discipline. Or rather, Horrid Talons is a discipline, which Claws of the Unholy causes to do aggravated damage. Either way, it would definitely do bashing to a strix. That's pretty black and white in the text. Whether a cruac ritual counts as a discipline is a little fuzzier, but generally I'd say it did. So, again, bashing. <br /> <br /> The fact that they're physical doesn't matter, because the rules say<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are completely immune to all physical and ephemeral attacks except for Disciplines and Devotions that inflict aggravated damage </div> </div> </div>.<br /> &quot;Physical and ephemeral&quot; there is one thing. They're immune to <i>everything</i>, unless it causes aggravated, so whether it was physical or not doesn't matter. They make no distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:11:24-08:00","id":782427,"title":"","content":"Blood and Smoke refers to Cruac and Theban Sorcery as Disciplines fairly consistently. By RAW rituals like Feeding the Crone would do bashing damage to the Strix. Whether the Discipline's damage is physical or ephemeral doesn't play into it. The Strix aren't made from Ephemera and their natural state isn't in Twilight.<br /> <br /> At least that's my read of the rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-08-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T22:04:20-08:00","id":782626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage?p=782162#post782162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that they're physical doesn't matter, because the rules say &quot;Physical and ephemeral&quot; there is one thing. They're immune to <i>everything</i>, unless it causes aggravated, so whether it was physical or not doesn't matter. They make no distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is both a solid understanding of the rules as written and how punctuation works in the English language. + 1 internet to you.<br /> <br /> I would say as written though, the two factors that are important is that it is a vampire Discipline or Devotion AND does aggravated damage, leaving the troubling thought of how non-vampires would deal with them since they are not ghost, spirits and are immune to everything (except vampire devotions and disciplines that do Agg, which thank you very much only do bashing now).<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember how some Storytellers used &quot;out-of-context&quot; antagonists to make vampires have a harder time dealing with them? Well that is nothing, now vampires are what you need to deal with Strix, and your werewolf is literally helpless against it.<br /> <br /> I don't think that is unfair even, and may be by design to give each venue something that they are needed to handle.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T02:27:23-08:00","id":782697,"title":"","content":"Much like the term &quot;Blood Potency&quot; can be substituted for any other supernatural tolerance trait, I generally assume &quot;discipline&quot; can be substituted for any equivalent sort of power. Gifts, Aracarna, Transmutations, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T02:30:41-08:00","id":782698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage?p=782626#post782626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember how some Storytellers used &quot;out-of-context&quot; antagonists to make vampires have a harder time dealing with them? Well that is nothing, now vampires are what you need to deal with Strix, and your werewolf is literally helpless against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The proverbial Moros would disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T04:09:50-08:00","id":782723,"title":"","content":"Also Fire. Werewolves can do fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T04:44:59-08:00","id":782733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage?p=782723#post782723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Fire. Werewolves can do fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of fire.<br /> <br /> Insane lots of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T04:56:03-08:00","id":782736,"title":"","content":"Everyone can deal with the strix by trapping them in a physical body or circle and setting it on fire. Strix also often come with individual banes that anyone can discover and exploit. Mind control is also effective, unless it happens to have a specific power. Shadow manipulators can do some things (including Obtenebration, psychic powers, and death magic) but the exact details have never been really explained, so that's up to ST fiat at this point.<br /> <br /> By the same token, however, everyone can deal with ghosts, spirits, angels, and goetics by their weaknesses or mind control. So its a moot point, all is said and done.<br /> <br /> But, that said, lets not get into a power measuring contest. Do we need to go into Obtenebration v. spirits and the like? Its just unnecessary to start saying that this or that power is required. Not to mention a large assumption - not every werewolf out there carries around fire elemental magic, so assuming that they'll have it in case they happen to run across one of the Owls of Dis is a bit of a stretch. Just like we can't assume every mage will have sufficent Death magic, every psychic can control shadows or flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-09-2015, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T05:43:23-08:00","id":782746,"title":"","content":"Do Strix even count as undead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T06:17:31-08:00","id":782754,"title":"","content":"No, but death magic includes shadow manipulation, which is explicitly noted to work on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T06:40:32-08:00","id":782767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage?p=782754#post782754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but death magic includes shadow manipulation, which is explicitly noted to work on them.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. They're not ghosts, they're not undead, but they can be manipulated through shadow-powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T09:27:41-08:00","id":782860,"title":"","content":"I was asking for another reason, I know Death's purview include shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T10:05:22-08:00","id":782890,"title":"","content":"I do think they'd count as something 'death-infused,' or resonant. 'Strix are creatures of death and impending doom,' it's why they find it easier to enter the bodies of the dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2015, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T10:55:24-08:00","id":782925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779658-strix-shadow-form-and-damage?p=782736#post782736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token, however, everyone can deal with ghosts, spirits, angels, and goetics by their weaknesses or mind control. So its a moot point, all is said and done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very valid point, I do like how the game developers have re-balanced things back towards an investigative horror game, where running and gunning with powers and weapons can be less effective than knowing what is going on and what to do.<br /> <br /> I've seen some 1 ed games that reminded me of Counter Strike with supernatural powers, with the classic most effective plan was &quot;Get 'em Ray&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}